stafford uneven district council is  currently consulting on its side  allocations plan and this short video  explains some of the proposals relating  to the centers of bidford or aven and  studly  within bidford proposal bid 1 seeks the  provision of a new center for the  village to the east of waterloo road and  south of wellington road  this is in recognition of the fact that  in recent years much of the development  in the village has been to the north of  the historic high street  which is now at the southern edge of the  village rather than at its heart  the proposed new centre is suggested to  include public space and a mix of shops  business commercial community and  educational uses  by focusing local facilities in a  location where they can be better  accessed will help the support a  thriving local economy  it is hoped that the proposal will also  help to revitalize the historic high  street as a destination for leisure  related retail activities  moving on to studly there are two  proposals within the site allocations  plan affecting the centre of the village  proposal stud1 proposes the location of  a new civic center to the south of the  high street  to include a range of uses such as  community business commercial  education and service facilities  proposals could also include an  enterprise centre providing specialist  workspace for local entrepreneurs  working or starting out in the digital  or creative sectors  as part of any development it will be  important to ensure that all existing  uses  and owners and occupiers on the site are  retained but in improved  premises benefiting both the businesses  and the wider village  delivery of the proposal will rely upon  the willingness of landowners  and the council will work with them and  the parish to deliver this  parish council to deliver this proposal  the second proposal within study center  stud ii  relates to the site adjacent to the  cooperative store on the high street  which has  been derelict for over 10 years the  council proposes to support the  redevelopment of this site to attract  businesses and jobs  provide affordable homes and improve the  environment of the centre  creating an attractive frontage to the  high street  you can find out more on each of these  proposals within bedford and studly  centres by viewing the site allocations  plan on our website  at www.stratford.gov dot uk  forward slash sapo where you can also  find out how to make your comments  we look forward to hearing what you  think about our proposals
 

